                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_340">London,
                            London, Carmelite convent</orgName> <p>This attribution was rejected in
                            the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which
                            did not change in the Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval
                            Libraries of Great Britain index card records the following information,
                            which was deemed unsatisfactory for an attribution:</p> <p>On page 96 is
                            <q>Iste altare dedicatur in honore sancte et indiuidue trinitatis et
                            gloriose uirginis Marie sancte Ieronimi beati Martini sanctique
                            Benedicti et omnium sanctorum. Et est titulus cuiusdam super altarius de
                            marmore lato quem Joh' Goldington sanctificari fecit tempore Willelmi
                            Woketon prioris qui die [...] unum aliud consecrari constituit de
                            alabastro in honore apostolorum Petri et Paul et est similiter
                            magnum.</q> Long erasure on p. 142.</p></provenance>
                    </history>
